arams":[{"description":"Raw reply, streamed with `text/csv`.","name":"response","type":{"names":["FastifyReply<import(\"fastify\").RouteGenericInterface, import(\"fastify\").RawServerDefault, import(\"http\").IncomingMessage, import(\"http\").ServerResponse<import(\"http\").IncomingMessage>, unknown, import(\"fastify\").FastifySchema, import(\"fastify\").FastifyTypeProviderDefault, unknown>"]}},{"description":"Rows and csv-stringify options.","name":"body","type":{"names":["{ records: (Record<string, unknown> | unknown[])[]; options?: { [x: string]: any; bom?: boolean; columns?: (string | { key: string; header?: string; })[]; eof?: boolean; escape?: string; escape_formulas?: boolean; header?: boolean; header_as_comment?: boolean; quote?: string | false; quote_record_delimiter?: boolean; quoted?: boolean; quoted_empty?: boolean; quoted_string?: boolean; }; }"]}}],"returns":[{"description":"CSV bytes.","type":{"names":["Promise<void>"]}}],"meta":{"lineno":82},"order":1,"mdaics":{"dist":"packages/backend/dist/resources/csv/csv.controller.js:27","src":"packages/backend/src/resources/csv/csv.controller.ts:49"},"level":0},{"id":"CsvController#extract","longname":"CsvController#extract","name":"extract","kind":"function","scope":"instance","description":"Parses an uploaded CSV into typed JSON records.","memberof":"CsvController","params":[{"description":"Flat csv-parse options.","name":"query","type":{"names":["{ [x: string]: any; bom?: boolean; cast?: boolean; cast_date?: boolean; columns?: boolean | string[] | any[]; comment?: string; comment_no_infix?: boolean; delimiter_auto?: boolean; encoding?: \"ascii\" | \"utf8\" | \"utf16le\" | \"ucs2\" | \"base64\" | \"latin1\" | \"binary\" | \"hex\"; escape?: string; from?: number; from_line?: number; group_columns_by_name?: boolean; ignore_last_delimiters?: boolean; ltrim?: boolean; max_record_size?: number; quote?: string | false; relax_column_count?: boolean; relax_column_count_less?: boolean; relax_column_count_more?: boolean; relax_quotes?: boolean; rtrim?: boolean; skip_empty_lines?: boolean; skip_records_with_empty_values?: boolean; skip_records_with_error?: boolean; to?: number; to_line?: number; trim?: boolean; }"]}}],"returns":[{"description":"The parsed records (201).","type":{"names":["Promise<{ records: unknown[]; }>"]}}],"meta":{"lineno":92},"order":2,"mdaics":{"dist":"packages/backend/dist/resources/csv/csv.controller.js:32","src":"packages/backend/src/resources/csv/csv.controller.ts:65"},"level":0},{"id":"CsvController#metadata","longname":"CsvController#metadata","name":"metadata","kind":"function","scope":"instance","description":"Structural CSV metadata: rows, columns, delimiter, per-column type census.","memberof":"CsvController","params":[{"description":"Flat csv-parse options plus `maxRows` for the type census.","name":"query","type":{"names":["{ [x: string]: any; maxRows: number; trim?: boolean; bom?: boolean; escape?: string; quote?: string | false; cast_date?: boolean; comment?: string; comment_no_infix?: boolean; delimiter_auto?: boolean; encoding?: \"ascii\" | \"utf8\" | \"utf16le\" | \"ucs2\" | \"base64\" | \"latin1\" | \"binary\" | \"hex\"; max_record_size?: number; relax_column_count?: boolean; relax_column_count_less?: boolean; relax_column_count_more?: boolean; relax_quotes?: boolean; skip_empty_lines?: boolean; }"]}}],"returns":[{"description":"The metadata document (201).","type":{"names":["Promise<{ bom: boolean; columns: number; delimiter: string | string[] | Buffer<ArrayBufferLike> | Buffer<ArrayBufferLike>[]; maxRows: number; perColumn: { index: number; types: Record<\"string\" | \"number\" | \"boolean\" | \"date\" | \"empty\", number>; }[]; recordDelimiter: string | string[] | Buffer<ArrayBufferLike> | Buffer<ArrayBufferLike>[]; rows: number; truncatedTypes: boolean; }>"]}}],"meta":{"lineno":100},"order":3,"mdaics":{"dist":"packages/backend/dist/resources/csv/csv.controller.js:35","src":"packages/backend/src/resources/csv/csv.controller.ts:78"},"level":0}],"fp":"b09add106da94d9d0962e0eb850e0b8c2df063974830b9db3b3f236eddf18597","issues":[],"kind":"tdata","lastUsed":1795079874861,"symbols":0},"md:packages/backend/src/resources/csv/csv.controller.ts":{"fp":"27a75a1b0b1dd0d69f348aa0962347a11d4e319f2b16290fb057be2a45d674ba","issues":[],"kind":"md","markdown":"<a name=\"CsvController\"></a>\n\n## CsvController\nCSV routes. Unlike the media modules this controller binds interceptors\nper route: `/csv/build` consumes a JSON body (the media parser never sees it),\nwhile `/csv/extract` and `/csv/metadata` take the binary upload and are\nClamAV-scanned like any other binary payload.\n\n**Kind**: global variable  \nsrc: packages/backend/src/resources/csv/csv.controller.ts:36  \ndist: packages/backend/dist/resources/csv/csv.controller.js:20\n\n* [CsvController](#CsvController)\n    * [.build(response, body)](#CsvController+build) ⇒ <code>Promise&lt;void&gt;</code>\n    * [.extract(query)](#CsvController+extract) ⇒ <code>Promise&lt;{ records: unknown[]; }&gt;</code>\n    * [.metadata(query)](#CsvController+metadata) ⇒ <code>Promise&lt;{ bom: boolean; columns: number; delimiter: string \\| string[] \\| Buffer&lt;ArrayBufferLike&gt; \\| Buffer&lt;ArrayBufferLike&gt;[]; maxRows: number; perColumn: { index: number; types: Record&lt;&quot;string&quot; \\| &quot;number&quot; \\| &quot;boolean&quot; \\| &quot;date&quot; \\| &quot;empty&quot;, number&gt;; }[]; recordDelimiter: string \\| string[] \\| Buffer&lt;ArrayBufferLike&gt; \\| Buffer&lt;ArrayBufferLike&gt;[]; rows: number; truncatedTypes: boolean; }&gt;</code>\n\n<a name=\"CsvController+build\"></a>\n\n### csvController.build(response, body) ⇒ <code>Promise&lt;void&gt;</code>\nSerializes JSON rows to CSV. POST-only: there is no meaningful GET shape.\n\n**Kind**: instance method of [<code>CsvController</code>](#CsvController)  \n**Returns**: <code>Promise&lt;void&gt;</code> - CSV bytes.  \n\n| Param | Type | Description |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| response | <code>FastifyReply&lt;import(&quot;fastify&quot;).RouteGenericInterface, import(&quot;fastify&quot;).RawServerDefault, import(&quot;http&quot;).IncomingMessage, import(&quot;http&quot;).ServerResponse&lt;import(&quot;http&quot;).IncomingMessage&gt;, unknown, import(&quot;fastify&quot;).FastifySchema, import(&quot;fastify&quot;).FastifyTypeProviderDefault, unknown&gt;</code> | Raw reply, streamed with `text/csv`. |\n| body | <code>{ records: (Record&lt;string, unknown&gt; \\| unknown[])[]; options?: { [x: string]: any; bom?: boolean; columns?: (string \\| { key: string; header?: string; })[]; eof?: boolean; escape?: string; escape\\_formulas?: boolean; header?: boolean; header\\_as\\_comment?: boolean; quote?: string \\| false; quote\\_record\\_delimiter?: boolean; quoted?: boolean; quoted\\_empty?: boolean; quoted\\_string?: boolean; }; }</code> | Rows and csv-stringify options. |\n\nsrc: packages/backend/src/resources/csv/csv.controller.ts:49  \ndist: packages/backend/dist/resources/csv/csv.controller.js:27\n<a name=\"CsvController+extract\"></a>\n\n### csvController.extract(query) ⇒ <code>Promise&lt;{ records: unknown[]; }&gt;</code>\nParses an uploaded CSV into typed JSON records.\n\n**Kind**: instance method of [<code>CsvController</code>](#CsvController)  \n**Returns**: <code>Promise&lt;{ records: unknown[]; }&gt;</code> - The parsed records (201).  \n\n| Param | Type | Description |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| query | <code>{ [x: string]: any; bom?: boolean; cast?: boolean; cast\\_date?: boolean; columns?: boolean \\| string[] \\| any[]; comment?: string; comment\\_no\\_infix?: boolean; delimiter\\_auto?: boolean; encoding?: &quot;ascii&quot; \\| &quot;utf8&quot; \\| &quot;utf16le&quot; \\| &quot;ucs2&quot; \\| &quot;base64&quot; \\| &quot;latin1&quot; \\| &quot;binary&quot; \\| &quot;hex&quot;; escape?: string; from?: number; from\\_line?: number; group\\_columns\\_by\\_name?: boolean; ignore\\_last\\_delimiters?: boolean; ltrim?: boolean; max\\_record\\_size?: number; quote?: string \\| false; relax\\_column\\_count?: boolean; relax\\_column\\_count\\_less?: boolean; relax\\_column\\_count\\_more?: boolean; relax\\_quotes?: boolean; rtrim?: boolean; skip\\_empty\\_lines?: boolean; skip\\_records\\_with\\_empty\\_values?: boolean; skip\\_records\\_with\\_error?: boolean; to?: number; to\\_line?: number; trim?: boolean; }</code> | Flat csv-parse options. |\n\nsrc: packages/backend/src/resources/csv/csv.controller.ts:65  \ndist: packages/backend/dist/resources/csv/csv.controller.js:32\n<a name=\"CsvController+metadata\"></a>\n\n### csvController.metadata(query) ⇒ <code>Promise&lt;{ bom: boolean; columns: number; delimiter: string \\| string[] \\| Buffer&lt;ArrayBufferLike&gt; \\| Buffer&lt;ArrayBufferLike&gt;[]; maxRows: number; perColumn: { index: number; types: Record&lt;&quot;string&quot; \\| &quot;number&quot; \\| &quot;boolean&quot; \\| &quot;date&quot; \\| &quot;empty&quot;, number&gt;; }[]; recordDelimiter: string \\| string[] \\| Buffer&lt;ArrayBufferLike&gt; \\| Buffer&lt;ArrayBufferLike&gt;[]; rows: number; truncatedTypes: boolean; }&gt;</code>\nStructural CSV metadata: rows, columns, delimiter, per-column type census.\n\n**Kind**: instance method of [<code>CsvController</code>](#CsvController)  \n**Returns**: <code>Promise&lt;{ bom: boolean; columns: number; delimiter: string \\| string[] \\| Buffer&lt;ArrayBufferLike&gt; \\| Buffer&lt;ArrayBufferLike&gt;[]; maxRows: number; perColumn: { index: number; types: Record&lt;&quot;string&quot; \\| &quot;number&quot; \\| &quot;boolean&quot; \\| &quot;date&quot; \\| &quot;empty&quot;, number&gt;; }[]; recordDelimiter: string \\| string[] \\| Buffer&lt;ArrayBufferLike&gt; \\| Buffer&lt;ArrayBufferLike&gt;[]; rows: number; truncatedTypes: boolean; }&gt;</code> - The metadata document (201).  \n\n| Param | Type | Description |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| query | <code>{ [x: string]: any; maxRows: number; trim?: boolean; bom?: boolean; escape?: string; quote?: string \\| false; cast\\_date?: boolean; 