ription":"Empty query object; junk parameters are rejected with 400.","name":"_query","type":{"names":["unknown"]}}],"returns":[{"description":"The metadata document.","type":{"names":["Promise<any>"]}}],"meta":{"lineno":101},"order":3,"mdaics":{"dist":"packages/backend/dist/resources/docx/docx.controller.js:37","src":"packages/backend/src/resources/docx/docx.controller.ts:74"},"level":0}],"fp":"8ccee8be27e065c765fd5014bc9f036d969c32b387b881b83edbe9c480cbf9af","issues":[],"kind":"tdata","lastUsed":1795079875058,"symbols":0},"md:packages/backend/src/resources/docx/docx.controller.spec.ts":{"fp":"6fce7ee251281f53a3a39ec216a1f6129b20b9993d5fa316e07c7558add46173","issues":["dist file not found — dist: line omitted (build first)"],"kind":"md","markdown":"<a name=\"rawSink\"></a>\n\n## rawSink() ⇒ <code>Writable &amp; { setHeader: ReturnType&lt;typeof vi.fn&gt;; }</code>\nCreates a Writable raw sink with `setHeader` mocks for assertions.\n\n**Kind**: global function  \n**Returns**: <code>Writable &amp; { setHeader: ReturnType&lt;typeof vi.fn&gt;; }</code> - A writable with a mocked `setHeader`.  \nsrc: packages/backend/src/resources/docx/docx.controller.spec.ts:10  \n","symbols":1,"lastUsed":1795079875050},"md:packages/backend/src/resources/docx/docx.controller.ts":{"fp":"73fbd11381a9243a6297ab68c2b7d54c40f74ecd3d895e437f36ec1c2d5a7ca7","issues":[],"kind":"md","markdown":"<a name=\"DocxController\"></a>\n\n## DocxController\nDOCX routes. `/docx/build` consumes JSON and bypasses the media\ninterceptors by design (JSON bodies are never virus-scanned or signature-probed);\n`/docx/extract` and `/docx/metadata` take the binary upload and are ClamAV-scanned.\n\n**Kind**: global variable  \nsrc: packages/backend/src/resources/docx/docx.controller.ts:29  \ndist: packages/backend/dist/resources/docx/docx.controller.js:21\n\n* [DocxController](#DocxController)\n    * [.build(response, body)](#DocxController+build) ⇒ <code>Promise&lt;void&gt;</code>\n    * [.extract(_query)](#DocxController+extract) ⇒ <code>Promise&lt;{ format: string; metadata: any; structure: { headings: { level: number; text: string; }[]; hyperlinks: any; images: { alts: string[]; count: number; }; lists: number; tables: any; }; text: string; }&gt;</code>\n    * [.metadata(_query)](#DocxController+metadata) ⇒ <code>Promise&lt;any&gt;</code>\n\n<a name=\"DocxController+build\"></a>\n\n### docxController.build(response, body) ⇒ <code>Promise&lt;void&gt;</code>\nBuilds a .docx from the JSON payload (201).\n\n**Kind**: instance method of [<code>DocxController</code>](#DocxController)  \n**Returns**: <code>Promise&lt;void&gt;</code> - The document bytes (201).  \n\n| Param | Type | Description |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| response | <code>FastifyReply&lt;import(&quot;fastify&quot;).RouteGenericInterface, import(&quot;fastify&quot;).RawServerDefault, import(&quot;http&quot;).IncomingMessage, import(&quot;http&quot;).ServerResponse&lt;import(&quot;http&quot;).IncomingMessage&gt;, unknown, import(&quot;fastify&quot;).FastifySchema, import(&quot;fastify&quot;).FastifyTypeProviderDefault, unknown&gt;</code> | Raw reply, streamed as .docx. |\n| body | <code>{ sections: { children: ({ runs: { [x: string]: any; text: string; allCaps?: boolean; bold?: boolean; break?: number; doubleStrike?: boolean; endnote?: number; footnote?: number; highlight?: &quot;black&quot; \\| &quot;blue&quot; \\| &quot;cyan&quot; \\| &quot;darkBlue&quot; \\| &quot;darkCyan&quot; \\| &quot;darkGray&quot; \\| &quot;darkGreen&quot; \\| &quot;darkMagenta&quot; \\| &quot;darkRed&quot; \\| &quot;darkYellow&quot; \\| &quot;green&quot; \\| &quot;lightGray&quot; \\| &quot;magenta&quot; \\| &quot;none&quot; \\| &quot;red&quot; \\| &quot;white&quot; \\| &quot;yellow&quot;; italics?: boolean; language?: string; smallCaps?: boolean; strike?: boolean; subScript?: boolean; superScript?: boolean; type?: &quot;run&quot;; underline?: true \\| { [x: string]: any; type: &quot;none&quot; \\| &quot;single&quot; \\| &quot;words&quot; \\