tring; }; numbering?: { [x: string]: any; levels: { format: &quot;none&quot; \\| &quot;decimal&quot; \\| &quot;upperRoman&quot; \\| &quot;lowerRoman&quot; \\| &quot;upperLetter&quot; \\| &quot;lowerLetter&quot; \\| &quot;bullet&quot;; level: number; alignment?: &quot;left&quot; \\| &quot;center&quot; \\| &quot;right&quot;; start?: number; text?: string; }[]; }[]; }</code> | Validated build payload. |\n\nsrc: packages/backend/src/resources/docx/docx.service.ts:365  \ndist: packages/backend/dist/resources/docx/docx.service.js:376 (approx.)\n<a name=\"DocxService+extract\"></a>\n\n### docxService.extract() ⇒ <code>Promise&lt;{ format: string; metadata: any; structure: { headings: { level: number; text: string; }[]; hyperlinks: any; images: { alts: string[]; count: number; }; lists: number; tables: any; }; text: string; }&gt;</code>\nExtracts text and structure from an uploaded .docx.\n\n**Kind**: instance method of [<code>DocxService</code>](#DocxService)  \n**Returns**: <code>Promise&lt;{ format: string; metadata: any; structure: { headings: { level: number; text: string; }[]; hyperlinks: any; images: { alts: string[]; count: number; }; lists: number; tables: any; }; text: string; }&gt;</code> - The parsed metadata, structure summary and full body text.  \nsrc: packages/backend/src/resources/docx/docx.service.ts:390  \ndist: packages/backend/dist/resources/docx/docx.service.js:401 (approx.)\n<a name=\"DocxService+metadata\"></a>\n\n### docxService.metadata() ⇒ <code>Promise&lt;any&gt;</code>\nNormalized OOXML metadata for an uploaded .docx.\n\n**Kind**: instance method of [<code>DocxService</code>](#DocxService)  \n**Returns**: <code>Promise&lt;any&gt;</code> - Format plus the parsed properties.  \nsrc: packages/backend/src/resources/docx/docx.service.ts:417  \ndist: packages/backend/dist/resources/docx/docx.service.js:422 (approx.)\n<a name=\"readPartsCapped\"></a>\n\n## readPartsCapped(buffer, limits) ⇒\nMaps the shared OOXML reader's cap violations to HTTP errors (413 for size, 400 otherwise).\n\n**Kind**: global function  \n**Returns**: The extracted package parts.  \n\n| Param | Type | Description |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| buffer | <code>Buffer&lt;ArrayBufferLike&gt;</code> | The buffered upload. |\n| limits |  | Optional per-call cap overrides. |\n\nsrc: packages/backend/src/resources/docx/docx.service.ts:28  \ndist: packages/backend/dist/resources/docx/docx.service.js:23\n<a name=\"readBody\"></a>\n\n## readBody(cls) ⇒ <code>Promise&lt;Buffer&lt;ArrayBufferLike&gt;&gt;</code>\nOpens the uploaded body, bounded by the scanner cap.\nThe scanner only opens the source when ClamAV is enabled, so the service must too.\n\n**Kind**: global function  \n**Returns**: <code>Promise&lt;Buffer&lt;ArrayBufferLike&gt;&gt;</code> - The body bytes, capped.  \n\n| Param | Type | Description |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| cls | <code>NormalizedClsService</code> | Normalized request context. |\n\nsrc: packages/backend/src/resources/docx/docx.service.ts:49  \ndist: packages/backend/dist/resources/docx/docx.service.js:36\n<a name=\"assertDocxSignature\"></a>\n\n## assertDocxSignature(buffer) ⇒ <code>Promise&lt;void&gt;</code>\nSignature must be the plain docx mime; closes the renamed-image and .docm/.dotx holes.\n\n**Kind**: global function  \n**Returns**: <code>Promise&lt;void&gt;</code> - Nothing when the signature is confirmed.  \n**Throws**:\n\n- <code>UnsupportedMediaTypeException</code> For non-docx signatures and mismatches.\n\n\n| Param | Type | Description |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| buffer | <code>Buffer&lt;ArrayBufferLike&gt;</code> | The buffered upload. |\n\nsrc: packages/backend/src/resources/docx/docx.service.ts:69  \ndist: packages/backend/dist/resources/docx/docx.service.js:49\n<a name=\"assertUniqueIds\"></a>\n\n## assertUniqueIds(body) ⇒ <code>{ commentIds: Set&lt;number&gt;; endnoteIds: Set&lt;number&gt;; noteIds: Set&lt;number&gt;; }</code>\nCollects and rejects duplicate note/comment ids.\n\n**Kind**: global function  \n**Returns*