"></a>\n\n## SHARP\\_TO\\_MIME\nResponse content-type per sharp-encodable format. `avif`/`jpg` are not\nencoder keys; formats absent from this map fall back to octet-stream.\n\n**Kind**: global constant  \nsrc: packages/backend/src/resources/image/image.controller.ts:29  \ndist: packages/backend/dist/resources/image/image.controller.js:22\n","symbols":2,"lastUsed":1795079891017},"tdata:packages/backend/src/resources/image/image.module.ts":{"doclets":[{"id":"ImageModule","longname":"ImageModule","name":"ImageModule","kind":"member","scope":"global","description":"Image feature module: processor, metadata, DNA, stats and OCR routes.","params":[],"meta":{"lineno":44},"order":0,"mdaics":{"dist":"packages/backend/dist/resources/image/image.module.js:27","src":"packages/backend/src/resources/image/image.module.ts:24"},"level":0}],"fp":"d922fb8de501225c170b3911f6f2848d4129fd75fd269f8aa4440e5a9d5fe5be","issues":[],"kind":"tdata","symbols":0,"lastUsed":1795079890880},"md:packages/backend/src/resources/image/image.module.ts":{"fp":"ce70a6ca433f0ba5e7e27e1476eab3d4cce1aea8464d19a2007245a48035f3f3","issues":[],"kind":"md","markdown":"<a name=\"ImageModule\"></a>\n\n## ImageModule\nImage feature module: processor, metadata, DNA, stats and OCR routes.\n\n**Kind**: global variable  \nsrc: packages/backend/src/resources/image/image.module.ts:24  \ndist: packages/backend/dist/resources/image/image.module.js:27\n","symbols":1,"lastUsed":1795079890937},"tdata:packages/backend/src/resources/image/image.service.spec.ts":{"doclets":[{"id":"TINY_PNG","longname":"TINY_PNG","name":"TINY_PNG","kind":"constant","scope":"global","description":"1x1 white PNG, decodes with the production preprocess pipeline.","params":[],"meta":{"lineno":6},"order":0,"mdaics":{"src":"packages/backend/src/resources/image/image.service.spec.ts:10"},"level":0},{"id":"makeService","longname":"makeService","name":"makeService","kind":"function","scope":"global","description":"Builds an ImageService with stubbed dependencies.","params":[{"description":"File signature returned by the stubbed CLS store.","name":"signature","type":{"names":["unknown"]}},{"description":"Factory opening a fresh input stream per call.","name":"source","type":{"names":["() => Readable"]}},{"description":"Whether the stubbed file-type check passes.","name":"isImage","defaultvalue":true,"type":{"names":["boolean"]}}],"returns":[{"description":"The service plus captured recognize calls for assertions.","type":{"names":["{ recognizeCalls: [Buffer<ArrayBufferLike>, string[]][]; service: ImageService; workerService: { createWorker: import(\"vitest\").Mock<() => Promise<Readable>>; }; }"]}}],"meta":{"lineno":21},"order":1,"mdaics":{"src":"packages/backend/src/resources/image/image.service.spec.ts:30"},"level":0}],"fp":"6b6142ee92e3658ebdb49a8ce5b390045782bb512746a323b7e7acb4bda45abb","issues":[],"kind":"tdata","lastUsed":1795079890815,"symbols":0},"md:packages/backend/src/resources/image/image.service.spec.ts":{"fp":"61fc272e08b96869373a57e05eda94e943dd745f2602b8d9a65edcc61044b1cc","issues":["dist file not found — dist: line omitted (build first)"],"kind":"md","markdown":"## Constants\n\n<dl>\n<dt><a href=\"#TINY_PNG\">TINY_PNG</a></dt>\n<dd><p>1x1 white PNG, decodes with the production preprocess pipeline.</p>\n</dd>\n</dl>\n\n## Functions\n\n<dl>\n<dt><a href=\"#makeService\">makeService(signature, source, isImage)</a> ⇒ <code>{ recognizeCalls: [Buffer&lt;ArrayBufferLike&gt;, string[]][]; service: ImageService; workerService: { createWorker: import(&quot;vitest&quot;).Mock&lt;() &#x3D;&gt; Promise&lt;Readable&gt;&gt;; }; }</code></dt>\n<dd><p>Builds an ImageService with stubbed dependencies.</p>\n</dd>\n</dl>\n\n<a name=\"TINY_PNG\"></a>\n\n## TINY\\_PNG\n1x1 white PNG, decodes with the production preprocess pipeline.\n\n**Kind**: global constant  \nsrc: packages/backend/src/resources/image/image.service.spec.ts:10  \n<a name=\"makeService\"></a>\n\n## makeService(signature, source, isImage) ⇒ <code>{ recognizeCalls: [Buffer&lt;ArrayBufferLike&gt;, string[]][]; service: ImageService; workerService: { createWorker: import(&quot;vitest&quot;).Mock&lt;() &#x3D;&gt; Promise&lt;Readable&gt;&gt;; }; }</code>\nBuilds an ImageService with stubbed dependencies.\n\n**Kind**: global function  \n**Returns**: <code>{ recognizeCalls: [Buffer&lt;ArrayBufferLike&gt;, string[]][]; service: ImageService; workerService: { createWorker: import(&quot;vitest&quot;).Mock&lt;() &#x3D;&gt; Promise&lt;Readable&gt;&gt;; }; }</code> - The service plus captured recognize calls for assertions.  \n\n| Param | Type | Default | Description |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| signature | <code>unknown</code> |  | File signature returned by the stubbed CLS store. |\n| source | <code>() &#x3D;&gt; Readable</code> |  | Factory opening a fresh input stream per call. |\n| isImage | <code>boolean</code> | <code>true</code> | Whether the stubbed file-type check passes. |\n\nsrc: packages/backend/src/resources/image/image.service.spec.ts:30  \n","symbols":2,"lastUsed":1795079890879},"tdata:packages/backend/src/resources/image/image.service.ts":{"doclets":[{"id":"ImageService","longname":"ImageService","name":"ImageService","kind":"member","scope":"global","description":"Image feature service: streams uploads through sharp workers for processing, metadata, DNA, stats and OCR.","params":[],"meta":{"lineno":42},"order":0,"mdaics":{"dist":"packages/backend/dist/resources/image/image.service.js:42 (approx.)","src":"packages/backend/src/resources/image/image.service.ts:20"},"level":0},{"id":"ImageService#parseLangs","longname":"ImageService#parseLangs","name":"parseLangs","kind":"function","scope":"instance","description":"Normalizes the `lang` query value: splits on `+` or `,`, lowercases,\ntrims, dedupes, sorts; defaults to `['eng']`, caps at 4 codes.","memberof":"ImageService","params":[{"description":"Raw `lang` query parameter (already regex-validated).","name":"raw","type":{"names":["string"]}}],"returns":[{"description":"Sorted, deduped language codes.","type":{"names":["string[]"]}}],"meta":{"lineno":138},"order":1,"mdaics":{"dist":"packages/backend/dist/resources/image/image.service.js:138 (approx.)","src":"packages/backend/src/resources/image/image.service.ts:110"},"level":0},{"id":"ImageService#preprocess","longname":"ImageService#preprocess","name":"preprocess","kind":"function","scope":"instance","description":"Preprocesses an image for OCR: auto-orient, downscale to at most 2000 px\nwithout enlarging, greyscale, normalize, sharpen; encoded as PNG.\nPixel bombs are rejected via `limitInputPixels`; undecodable or malicious\ninput surfaces as {@link UnsupportedMediaTypeException} instead of a 500.","memberof":"ImageService","params":[{"description":"Raw (signature-verified) image bytes.","name":"input","type":{"names":["Buffer<ArrayBufferLike>"]}}],"returns":[{"description":"PNG bytes ready for tesseract.","type":{"names":["Promise<Buffer<ArrayBufferLike>>"]}}],"meta":{"lineno":157},"async":true,"order":2,"mdaics":{"dist":"packages/backend/dist/resources/image/image.service.js:157 (approx.)","src":"packages/backend/src/resources/image/image.service.ts:131"},"level":0}],"fp":"d3e6a85145d4126e3f8e3fba577f54f336f1ee61d1fed68da57a48ee97ddda5e","issues":[],"kind":"tdata","lastUsed":1795079890879,"symbols":0},"tdata:packages/backend/src/resources/image/image.worker.spec.ts":{"doclets":[{"id":"tinyJpeg","longname":"tinyJpeg","name":"tinyJpeg","kind":"member","scope":"global","description":"A tiny synthetic JPEG (64x48, blue with a white 16x16 square): large enough\nfor every sharp operation in the worker, small enough to keep the suite fast\nand deterministic.","params":[],"meta":{"lineno":14},"order":0,"mdaics":{"src":"packages/backend/src/resources/image/image.worker.spec.ts:17"},"level":0},{"id":"capturingStdout","longname":"capturingStdout","name":"capturingStdout","kind":"function","scope":"global","description":"A capturing stdout Writable: `writes` accumulates chunks, `finished` resolves on `end`.","params":[],"returns":[{"description":"The writes, the sink and the completion promise.","type":{"names":["{ finished: Promise<void>; stdout: any; writes: Buffer<ArrayBufferLike>[]; }"]}}],"meta":{"lineno":30},"order":1,"mdaics":{"src":"packages/backend/src/resources/image/image.worker.spec.ts:35"},"level":0},{"id":"run","longname":"run","name":"run","kind":"function","scope":"global","description":"Points stdin/stdout at the tiny fixture and a capturing sink, then runs the worker with explicit data.","params":[{"description":"Worker-thread data (`operation` and optional payload) passed to the worker.","name":"data","type":{"names":["Record<string, unknown>"]}}],"returns":[{"description":"The captured stdout chunks.","type":{"names":["Promise<Buffer<ArrayBufferLike>[]>"]}}],"meta":{"lineno":52},"async":true,"order":2,"mdaics":{"src":"packages/backend/src/resources/image/image.worker.spec.ts:58"},"level":0}],"fp":"d4ac82f83f10520fcf27dce0e82b8137cab79f732006e9c5d5eccdb7e371f11e","issues":[],"kind":"tdata","lastUsed":1795079890937,"symbols":0},"md:packages/backend/src/resources/image/image.worker.spec.ts":{"fp":"082f5e4abde280f9fe5d72608be73d4aba8cbdd4b02334a3d9535609026e900b","issues":["dist file not found — dist: line omitted (build first)"],"kind":"md","markdown":"## Members\n\n<dl>\n<dt><a href=\"#tinyJpeg\">tinyJpeg</a></dt>\n<dd><p>A tiny synthetic JPEG (64x48, blue with a white 16x16 square): large enough\nfor every sharp operation in the worker, small enough to keep the suite fast\nand deterministic.</p>\n</dd>\n</dl>\n\n## Functions\n\n<dl>\n<dt><a href=\"#capturingStdout\">capturingStdout()</a> ⇒ <code>{ finished: Promise&lt;void&gt;; stdout: any; writes: Buffer&lt;ArrayBufferLike&gt;[]; }</code></dt>\n<dd><p>A capturing stdout Writable: <code>writes</code> accumulates chunks, <code>finished</code> resolves on <code>end</code>.</p>\n</dd>\n<dt><a href=\"#run\">run(data)</a> ⇒ <code>Promise&lt;Buffer&lt;ArrayBufferLike&gt;[]&gt;</code></dt>\n<dd><p>Points stdin/stdout at the tiny fixture and a capturing sink, then runs the worker with explicit data.</p>\n</dd>\n</dl>\n\n<a name=\"tinyJpeg\"></a>\n\n## tinyJpeg\nA tiny synthetic JPEG (64x48, blue with a white 16x16 square): large enough\nfor every sharp operation in the worker, small enough to keep the suite fast\nand deterministic.\n\n**Kind**: global variable  \nsrc: packages/backend/src/resources/image/image.worker.spec.ts:17  \n<a name=\"capturingStdout\"></a>\n\n## capturingStdout() ⇒ <code>{ finished: Promise&lt;void&gt;; stdout: any; writes: Buffer&lt;ArrayBufferLike&gt;[]; }</code>\nA capturing stdout Writable: `writes` accumulates chunks, `finished` resolves on `end`.\n\n**Kind**: global function  \n**Returns**: <code>{ finished: Promise&lt;void&gt;; stdout: any; writes: Buffer&lt;ArrayBufferLike&gt;[]; }</code> - The writes, the sink and the completion promise.  \nsrc: packages/backend/src/resources/image/image.worker.spec.ts:35  \n<a name=\"run\"></a>\n\n## run(data) ⇒ <code>Promise&lt;Buffer&lt;ArrayBufferLike&gt;[]&gt;</code>\nPoints stdin/stdout at the tiny fixture and a capturing sink, then runs the worker with explicit data.\n\n**Kind**: global function  \n**Returns**: <code>Promise&lt;Buffer&lt;ArrayBufferLike&gt;[]&gt;</code> - The captured stdout chunks.  \n\n| Param | Type | Description |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| data | <code>Record&lt;string, unknown&gt;</code> | Worker-thread data (`operation` and optional payload) passed to the worker. |\n\nsrc: packages/backend/src/resources/image/image.worker.spec.ts:58  \n","symbols":3,"lastUsed":1795079890968},"tdata:packages/backend/src/resources/image/schema.ts":{"doclets":[{"id":"positionKeys","longname":"positionKeys","name":"positionKeys","kind":"constant","scope":"global","description":"resize position accepts sharp's corner/edge names plus everything in sharp.gravity.","params":[],"meta":{"lineno":10},"order":0,"mdaics":{"dist":"packages/backend/dist/resources/image/schema.js:9","src":"packages/backend/src/resources/image/schema.ts:14"},"level":0},{"id":"ImageProcessorSchema","longname":"ImageProcessorSchema","name":"ImageProcessorSchema","kind":"constant","scope":"global","description":"Query parameters for `/image/processor`, `/image/metadata`, `/image/dna` and `/image/stats` uploads.","meta":{"lineno":17},"order":1,"mdaics":{"dist":"packages/backend/dist/resources/image/schema.js:15","src":"packages/backend/src/resources/image/schema.ts:23"},"level":0},{"id":"LANG_REGEX","longname":"LANG_REGEX","name":"LANG_REGEX","kind":"constant","scope":"global","description":"Case-insensitive language code pattern: a three-letter ISO 639-2 code\noptionally followed by a script suffix (`_latn`, `_cyrl`, ...). Codes are\ncombined with `+` or `,` (up to four). `+` only reaches this endpoint\nURL-encoded (`%2B`), because query-string decoders treat a raw `+` as a space.","params":[],"meta":{"lineno":48},"order":2,"mdaics":{"dist":"packages/backend/dist/resources/image/schema.js:48 (approx.)","src":"packages/backend/src/resources/image/schema.ts:58"},"level":0},{"id":"OcrSchema","longname":"OcrSchema","name":"OcrSchema","kind":"constant","scope":"global","description":"Query schema for the `/image/ocr` endpoint.","meta":{"lineno":52},"order":3,"mdaics":{"dist":"packages/backend/dist/resources/image/schema.js:40","src":"packages/backend/src/resources/image/schema.ts:63"},"level":0}],"fp":"842c2a4f4d4fba63a5508b8ddf9e01f71accfee9c59b11758bb156c5032291f9","issues":[],"kind":"tdata","lastUsed":1795079891017,"symbols":0},"md:packages/backend/src/resources/image/schema.ts":{"fp":"1f8fa082b8a0077258c0369f8244afaf798d2eb21a1e9be10cf21501f6ca538e","issues":["dist sourcemap missing or unmatched — dist line is an approximation"],"kind":"md","markdown":"## Constants\n\n<dl>\n<dt><a href=\"#positionKeys\">positionKeys</a></dt>\n<dd><p>resize position accepts sharp&#39;s corner/edge names plus everything in sharp.gravity.</p>\n</dd>\n<dt><a href=\"#ImageProcessorSchema\">ImageProcessorSchema</a></dt>\n<dd><p>Query parameters for <code>/image/processor</code>, <code>/image/metadata</code>, <code>/image/dna</code> and <code>/image/stats</code> uploads.</p>\n</dd>\n<dt><a href=\"#LANG_REGEX\">LANG_REGEX</a></dt>\n<dd><p>Case-insensitive language code pattern: a three-letter ISO 639-2 code\noptionally followed by a script suffix (<code>_latn</code>, <code>_cyrl</code>, ...). Codes are\ncombined with <code>+</code> or <code>,</code> (up to four). <code>+</code> only reaches this endpoint\nURL-encoded (<code>%2B</code>), because query-string decoders treat a raw <code>+</code> as a space.</p>\n</dd>\n<dt><a href=\"#OcrSchema\">OcrSchema</a></dt>\n<dd><p>Query schema for the <code>/image/ocr</code> endpoint.</p>\n</dd>\n</dl>\n\n<a name=\"positionKeys\"></a>\n\n## positionKeys\nresize position accepts sharp's corner/edge names plus everything in sharp.gravity.\n\n**Kind**: global constant  \nsrc: packages/backend/src/resources/image/schema.ts:14  \ndist: packages/backend/dist/resources/image/schema.js:9\n<a name=\"ImageProcessorSchema\"></a>\n\n## ImageProcessorSchema\nQuery parameters for `/image/processor`, `/image/metadata`, `/image/dna` and `/image/stats` uploads.\n\n**Kind**: global constant  \nsrc: packages/backend/src/resources/image/schema.ts:23  \ndist: packages/backend/dist/resources/image/schema.js:15\n<a name=\"LANG_REGEX\"></a>\n\n## LANG\\_REGEX\nCase-insensitive language code pattern: a three-letter ISO 639-2 code\noptionally followed by a script suffix (`_latn`, `_cyrl`, ...). Codes are\ncombined with `+` or `,` (up to four). `+` only reaches this endpoint\nURL-encoded (`%2B`), because query-string decoders treat a raw `+` as a space.\n\n**Kind**: global constant  \nsrc: packages/backend/src/resources/image/schema.ts:58  \ndist: packages/backend/dist/resources/image/schema.js:48 (approx.)\n<a name=\"OcrSchema\"></a>\n\n## OcrSchema\nQuery schema for the `/image/ocr` endpoint.\n\n**Kind**: global constant  \nsrc: packages/backend/src/resources/image/schema.ts:63  \ndist: packages/backend/dist/resources/image/schema.js:40\n","symbols":4,"lastUsed":1795079891078},"tdata:packages/backend/src/resources/image/tesseract.service.edge.spec.ts":{"doclets":[],"fp":"bbf634a4ab52ee2e768bf04ca3a9f82247c406c9f91d34f5f5f284adc34d363f","issues":[],"kind":"tdata","lastUsed":1795079891018,"symbols":0},"md:packages/backend/src/resources/image/tesseract.service.edge.spec.ts":{"fp":"0c051aa3b59e16011e2942358a3825b9096ff4207605780e1503234e05053afc","issues":["dist file not found — dist: line omitted (build first)"],"kind":"md","skipped":"no-jsdoc","symbols":0,"lastUsed":1795079891018},"tdata:packages/backend/src/resources/image/tesseract.service.spec.ts":{"doclets":[],"fp":"62de3c2f651dc3cb071843d74cab62906805ad3ddabd33f3be34170c5cbf137c","issues":[],"kind":"tdata","lastUsed":1795079891025,"symbols":0},"md:packages/backend/src/resources/image/tesseract.service.spec.ts":{"fp":"136ebbbcc42af8e21c1364f3b65efcf9a3f549439651eaae1216f5b55a4207b0","issues":["dist file not found — dist: line omitted (build first)"],"kind":"md","skipped":"no-jsdoc","symbols":0,"lastUsed":1795079891041},"tdata:packages/backend/src/resources/image/type.ts":{"doclets":[],"fp":"7c2e33acebebfb032af47a8decb01efc0812ddc4bde64e37ef9c0099e2d226fd","issues":[],"kind":"tdata","lastUsed":1795079891044,"symbols":0},"md:packages/backend/src/resources/image/type.ts":{"fp":"88e0a9fa5500ceee13da6db0566c878edab99a410f5033ee5a19bdbdbe3664db","issues":[],"kind":"md","skipped":"no-jsdoc","symbols":0,"lastUsed":1795079891079},"tdata:packages/backend/src/resources/image/worker/index.ts":{"doclets":[{"id":"finishWorker","longname":"finishWorker","name":"finishWorker","kind":"function","scope":"global","description":"Ends the worker process once the job is done: drops the stdin handle so\nthe event loop drains naturally, with a short backstop if native handles linger.","params":[{"description":"Exit code for the worker process.","name":"code","type":{"names":["number"]}}],"meta":{"lineno":12},"order":0,"mdaics":{"dist":"packages/backend/dist/resources/image/worker/index.js:7","src":"packages/backend/src/resources/image/worker/index.ts:18"},"level":0},{"id":"runImageWorker","longname":"runImageWorker","name":"runImageWorker","kind":"function","scope":"global","description":"Dispatches the requested image operation (processor/metadata/stats).","params":[{"description":"Worker dispatch data (defaults to the spawned worker's workerData).","name":"inputData","type":{"names":["ImageWorkerData"]}}],"meta":{"lineno":22},"order":1,"mdaics":{"dist":"packages/backend/dist/resources/image/worker/index.js:12","src":"packages/backend/src/resources/image/worker/index.ts:29"},"returns":[{"type":{"names":["Promise<void>"]}}],"level":0},{"id":"startImageWorker","longname":"startImageWorker","name":"startImageWorker","kind":"function","scope":"global","description":"Runs the worker job and, only inside a spawned worker thread, finishes the process.","returns":[{"description":"The job (with exit-code handling attached when running as a worker thread).","type":{"names":["Promise<any>"]}}],"meta":{"lineno":39},"order":2,"mdaics":{"dist":"packages/backend/dist/resources/image/worker/index.js:25","src":"packages/backend/src/resources/image/worker/index.ts:47"},"level":0}],"fp":"8a502b5e33304693d3f0a87e13fe4d6e42cab00b4ecadc07a949b45615caab35","issues":[],"kind":"tdata","lastUsed":1795079891079,"symbols":0},"md:packages/backend/src/resources/image/worker/index.ts":{"fp":"6ca4ad118aebabb860e8d6e87254af3172965c68f08ec46c7efc3328fdfd1b9a","issues":[],"kind":"md","markdown":"## Functions\n\n<dl>\n<dt><a href=\"#finishWorker\">finishWorker(code)</a></dt>\n<dd><p>Ends the worker process once the job is done: drops the stdin handle so\nthe event loop drains naturally, with a short backstop if native handles linger.</p>\n</dd>\n<dt><a href=\"#runImageWorker\">runImageWorker(inputData)</a> ⇒ <code>Promise&lt;void&gt;</code></dt>\n<dd><p>Dispatches the requested image operation (processor/metadata/stats).</p>\n</dd>\n<dt><a href=\"#startImageWorker\">startImageWorker()</a> ⇒ <code>Promise&lt;any&gt;</code></dt>\n<dd><p>Runs the worker job and, only inside a spawned worker thread, finishes the process.</p>\n</dd>\n</dl>\n\n<a name=\"finishWorker\"></a>\n\n## finishWorker(code)\nEnds the worker process once the job is done: drops the stdin handle so\nthe event loop drains naturally, with a short backstop if native handles linger.\n\n**Kind**: global function  \n\n| Param | Type | Description |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| code | <code>number</code> | Exit code for the worker process. |\n\nsrc: packages/backend/src/resources/image/worker/index.ts:18  \ndist: packages/backend/dist/resources/image/worker/index.js:7\n<a name=\"runImageWorker\"></a>\n\n## runImageWorker(inputData) ⇒ <code>Promise&lt;void&gt;</code>\nDispatches the requested image operation (processor/metadata/stats).\n\n**Kind**: global function  \n\n| Param | Type | Description |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| inputData | <code>ImageWorkerData</code> | Worker dispatch data (defaults to the spawned worker's workerData). |\n\nsrc: packages/backend/src/resources/image/worker/index.ts:29  \ndist: packages/backend/dist/resources/image/worker/index.js:12\n<a name=\"startImageWorker\"></a>\n\n## startImageWorker() ⇒ <code>Promise&lt;any&gt;</code>\nRuns the worker job and, only inside a spawned worker thread, finishes the process.\n\n**Kind**: global function  \n**Returns**: <code>Promise&lt;any&gt;</code> - The job (with exit-code handling attached when running as a worker thread).  \nsrc: packages/backend/src/resources/image/worker/index.ts:47  \ndist: packages/backend/dist/resources/image/worker/index.js:25\n","symbols":3,"lastUsed":1795079891118},"tdata:packages/backend/src/resources/image/tesseract.service.ts":{"doclets":[{"id":"TesseractService","longname":"TesseractService","name":"TesseractService","kind":"member","scope":"global","description":"Bounded pool of tesseract.js workers for `/image/ocr`; terminated on shutdown.","params":[],"meta":{"lineno":56},"order":1,"mdaics":{"dist":"packages/backend/dist/resources/image/tesseract.service.js:15","src":"packages/backend/src/resources/image/tesseract.service.ts:38"},"level":0},{"id":"SINGLE_LANG_REGEX","longname":"SINGLE_LANG_REGEX","name":"SINGLE_LANG_REGEX","kind":"constant","scope":"global","description":"ISO 639-2 language code with an optional script suffix — tesseract's on-disk layout (`<code>.traineddata`).","params":[],"meta":{"lineno":44},"order":0,"mdaics":{"dist":"packages/backend/dist/resources/image/tesseract.service.js:14","src":"packages/backend/src/resources/image/tesseract.service.ts:17"},"level":0},{"id":"TesseractService#onModuleDestroy","longname":"TesseractService#onModuleDestroy","name":"onModuleDestroy","kind":"function","scope":"instance","description":"Terminates every worker on shutdown and wakes pending acquire() callers\nso they fail fast with 503 instead of waiting for a slot forever.","memberof":"TesseractService","params":[],"meta":{"lineno":79},"async":true,"order":2,"mdaics":{"dist":"packages/backend/dist/resources/image/tesseract.service.js:21","src":"packages/backend/src/resources/image/tesseract.service.ts:49"},"returns":[{"type":{"names":["Promise<void>"]}}],"level":0},{"id":"TesseractService#onModuleInit","longname":"TesseractService#onModuleInit","name":"onModuleInit","kind":"function","scope":"instance","description":"Prepares the cache directory and warms the configured preload languages.","memberof":"TesseractService","params":[],"meta":{"lineno":90},"async":true,"order":3,"mdaics":{"dist":"packages/backend/dist/resources/image/tesseract.service.js:29","src":"packages/backend/src/resources/image/tesseract.service.ts:60"},"returns":[{"type":{"names":["Promise<void>"]}}],"level":0},{"id":"TesseractService#recognize","longname":"TesseractService#recognize","name":"recognize","kind":"function","scope":"instance","description":"Recognizes text in the given image buffer.","memberof":"TesseractService","params":[{"description":"Preprocessed (PNG) image bytes.","name":"buffer","type":{"names":["Buffer<ArrayBufferLike>"]}},{"description":"Language codes to use (already normalized).","name":"langs","type":{"names":["string[]"]}}],"returns":[{"description":"Text with a per-line breakdown, normalized languages, confidence and wall time.","type":{"names":["Promise<ImageOcrResult>"]}}],"meta":{"lineno":113},"async":true,"order":4,"mdaics":{"dist":"packages/backend/dist/resources/image/tesseract.service.js:45","src":"packages/backend/src/resources/image/tesseract.service.ts:84"},"level":0},{"id":"TesseractService#retire","longname":"TesseractService#retire","name":"retire","kind":"function","scope":"instance","description":"Terminates a slot and removes it from the pool, then wakes one waiter.","memberof":"TesseractService","params":[{"description":"Pool slot whose worker is being retired.","name":"slot","type":{"names":["Slot"]}}],"meta":{"lineno":171},"async":true,"order":5,"mdaics":{"dist":"packages/backend/dist/resources/image/tesseract.service.js:95","src":"packages/backend/src/resources/image/tesseract.service.ts:147"},"returns":[{"type":{"names":["Promise<void>"]}}],"level":0}],"fp":"182560014fb16a0006945173b239bb451f5a7f33e494d03fbc90e3ed8d87bf95","issues":[],"kind":"tdata","symbols":0,"lastUsed":1795079891341},"md:packages/backend/src/resources/image/tesseract.service.ts":{"fp":"974f13aa6e75c9f0e1749c9343a42a77b30fc0618c30b145714e5731dcd00411","issues":[],"kind":"md","markdown":"## Members\n\n<dl>\n<dt><a href=\"#TesseractService\">TesseractService</a></dt>\n<dd><p>Bounded pool of tesseract.js workers for <code>/image/ocr</code>; terminated on shutdown.</p>\n</dd>\n</dl>\n\n## Constants\n\n<dl>\n<dt><a href=\"#SINGLE_LANG_REGEX\">SINGLE_LANG_REGEX</a></dt>\n<dd><p>ISO 639-2 language code with an optional script suffix — tesseract&#39;s on-disk layout (<code>&lt;code&gt;.traineddata</code>).</p>\n</dd>\n</dl>\n\n<a name=\"TesseractService\"></a>\n\n## TesseractService\nBounded pool of tesseract.js workers for `/image/ocr`; terminated on shutdown.\n\n**Kind**: global variable  \nsrc: packages/backend/src/resources/image/tesseract.service.ts:38  \ndist: packages/backend/dist/resources/image/tesseract.service.js:15\n\n* [TesseractService](#TesseractService)\n    * [.onModuleDestroy()](#TesseractService+onModuleDestroy) ⇒ <code>Promise&lt;void&gt;</code>\n    * [.onModuleInit()](#TesseractService+onModuleInit) ⇒ <code>Promise&lt;void&gt;</code>\n    * [.recognize(buffer, langs)](#TesseractService+recognize) ⇒ <code>Promise&lt;ImageOcrResult&gt;</code>\n    * [.retire(slot)](#TesseractService+retire) ⇒ <code>Promise&lt;void&gt;</code>\n\n<a name=\"TesseractService+onModuleDestroy\"></a>\n\n### tesseractService.onModuleDestroy() ⇒ <code>Promise&lt;void&gt;</code>\nTerminates every worker on shutdown and wakes pending acquire() callers\nso they fail fast with 503 instead of waiting for a slot forever.\n\n**Kind**: instance method of [<code>TesseractService</code>](#TesseractService)  \nsrc: packages/backend/src/resources/image/tesseract.service.ts:49  \ndist: packages/backend/dist/resources/image/tesseract.service.js:21\n<a name=\"TesseractService+onModuleInit\"></a>\n\n### tesseractService.onModuleInit() ⇒ <code>Promise&lt;void&gt;</code>\nPrepares the cache directory and warms the configured preload languages.\n\n**Kind**: instance method of [<code>TesseractService</code>](#TesseractService)  \nsrc: packages/backend/src/resources/image/tesseract.service.ts:60  \ndist: packages/backend/dist/resources/image/tesseract.service.js:29\n<a name=\"TesseractService+recognize\"></a>\n\n### tesseractService.recognize(buffer, langs) ⇒ <code>Promise&lt;ImageOcrResult&gt;</code>\nRecognizes text in the given image buffer.\n\n**Kind**: instance method of [<code>TesseractService</code>](#TesseractService)  \n**Returns**: <code>Promise&lt;ImageOcrResult&gt;</code> - Text with a per-line breakdown, normalized languages, confidence and wall time.  \n\n| Param | Type | Description |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| buffer | <code>Buffer&lt;ArrayBufferLike&gt;</code> | Preprocessed (PNG) image bytes. |\n| langs | <code>string[]</code> | Language codes to use (already normalized). |\n\nsrc: packages/backend/src/resources/image/tesseract.service.ts:84  \ndist: packages/backend/dist/resources/image/tesseract.service.js:45\n<a name=\"TesseractService+retire\"></a>\n\n### tesseractService.retire(slot) ⇒ <code>Promise&lt;void&gt;</code>\nTerminates a slot and removes it from the pool, then wakes one waiter.\n\n**Kind**: instance method of [<code>TesseractService</code>](#TesseractService)  \n\n| Param | Type | Description |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| slot | <code>Slot</code> | Pool slot whose worker is being retired. |\n\nsrc: packages/backend/src/resources/image/tesseract.service.ts:147  \ndist: packages/backend/dist/resources/image/tesseract.service.js:95\n<a name=\"SINGLE_LANG_REGEX\"></a>\n\n## SINGLE\\_LANG\\_REGEX\nISO 639-2 language code with an optional script suffix — tesseract's on-disk layout (`<code>.traineddata`).\n\n**Kind**: global constant  \nsrc: packages/backend/src/resources/image/tesseract.service.ts:17  \ndist: packages/backend/dist/resources/image/tesseract.service.js:14\n","symbols":6,"lastUsed":1795079891425},"tdata:packages/backend/src/resources/image/worker/inspect.ts":{"doclets":[{"id":"Discard","longname":"Discard","name":"Discard","kind":"class","scope":"global","description":"A Writable that discards everything written to it, used to consume an image\nstream while sharp gathers metadata/stats (so the image bytes never reach stdout).","meta":{"lineno":8},"order":0,"mdaics":{"dist":"packages/backend/dist/resources/image/worker/inspect.js:4","src":"packages/backend/src/resources/image/worker/inspect.ts:9"},"level":0}],"fp":"b95a3dc48153211ea615a57029bcf845c1997bf73961ef79930a3262570e16d2","issues":[],"kind":"tdata","lastUsed":1795079891130,"symbols":0},"md:packages/backend/src/resources/image/worker/inspect.ts":{"fp":"f8ce6665a14bb14dadf4b1637461c3b8911befa096949f28ccc2db703063f345","issues":[],"kind":"md","markdown":"<a name=\"Discard\"></a>\n\n## Discard\nA Writable that discards everything written to it, used to consume an image\nstream while sharp gathers metadata/stats (so the image bytes never reach stdout).\n\n**Kind**: global class  \nsrc: packages/backend/src/resources/image/worker/inspect.ts:9  \ndist: packages/backend/dist/resources/image/worker/inspect.js:4\n","symbols":1,"lastUsed":1795079891162},"tdata:packages/backend/src/resources/image/worker/processor.spec.ts":{"doclets":[],"fp":"62ddeabf47db7ced121ffd9070ec277438f0b224ebb161452d15eb226ef49cd0","issues":[],"kind":"tdata","lastUsed":1795079891130,"symbols":0},"md:packages/backend/src/resources/image/worker/processor.spec.ts":{"fp":"d5b19de2dc01047ffb27198da7cc21fa1989fd8c0fdf2c7aea328e50400ed3ec","issues":["dist file not found — dist: line omitted (build first)"],"kind":"md","skipped":"no-jsdoc","symbols":0,"lastUsed":1795079891130},"tdata:packages/backend/src/resources/image/worker/processor.ts":{"doclets":[],"fp":"e0d634165457496cde7115c5afc292a3051bbd4f08a97046a08942b4ec372271","issues":[],"kind":"tdata","lastUsed":1795079891143,"symbols":0},"md:packages/backend/src/resources/image/worker/processor.ts":{"fp":"4a82cc18d7181f02c4ac35a925f79ad71bc880c8987888f39317c642498f35b0","issues":[],"kind":"md","skipped":"no-jsdoc","symbols":0,"lastUsed":1795079891184},"tdata:packages/backend/src/resources/image/worker/worker.spec.ts":{"doclets":[{"id":"importWorker","longname":"importWorker","name":"importWorker","kind":"function","scope":"global","description":"Imports the image worker fresh with the given workerData.","params":[{"description":"the worker payload (operation).","name":"workerData","type":{"names":["Record<string, unknown>"]}}],"meta":{"lineno":28},"async":true,"order":0,"mdaics":{"src":"packages/backend/src/resources/image/worker/worker.spec.ts:35"},"returns":[{"type":{"names":["Promise<void>"]}}],"level":0}],"fp":"1ccf1c447a6a4086348717960f50fad0fef6a8ea60d03bee3af4ef8c63627e6c","issues":[],"kind":"tdata","lastUsed":1795079891162,"symbols":0},"md:packages/backend/src/resources/image/worker/worker.spec.ts":{"fp":"880df2131813dcf241377e76511c81425964781f9b4e0db9d9a262d4c386f263","issues":["dist file not found — dist: line omitted (build first)"],"kind":"md","markdown":"<a name=\"importWorker\"></a>\n\n## importWorker(workerData) ⇒ <code>Promise&lt;void&gt;</code>\nImports the image worker fresh with the given workerData.\n\n**Kind**: global function  \n\n| Param | Type | Description |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| workerData | <code>Record&lt;string, unknown&gt;</code> | the worker payload (operation). |\n\nsrc: packages/backend/src/resources/image/worker/worker.spec.ts:35  \n","symbols":1,"lastUsed":1795079891183},"tdata:packages/backend/src/resources/model/gltf.ts":{"doclets":[{"id":"ioPromise","longname":"ioPromise","name":"ioPromise","kind":"member","scope":"global","description":"Lazily-built NodeIO with meshopt and draco registered; wasm modules are created once per process.","params":[],"meta":{"lineno":9},"order":0,"mdaics":{"dist":"packages/backend/dist/resources/model/gltf.js:7","src":"packages/backend/src/resources/model/gltf.ts:18"},"level":0},{"id":"readModel","longname":"readModel","name":"readModel","kind":"constant","scope":"global","description":"Opens a GLB work package; a single corrupt byte answers 400.","params":[{"description":"The uploaded GLB bytes.","name":"buffer","type":{"names":["Buffer<ArrayBufferLike>"]}}],"returns":[{"description":"The parsed gltf-transform document.","type":{"names":["Promise<Document>"]}}],"meta":{"lineno":36},"order":1,"mdaics":{"dist":"packages/backend/dist/resources/model/gltf.js:27","src":"packages/backend/src/resources/model/gltf.ts:47"},"level":0},{"id":"writeGlb","longname":"writeGlb","name":"writeGlb","kind":"constant","scope":"global","description":"Serializes a document to GLB bytes.","params":[{"description":"The document to serialize.","name":"document","type":{"names":["Document"]}}],"returns":[{"description":"The GLB bytes.","type":{"names":["Promise<Uint8Array<ArrayBufferLike>>"]}}],"meta":{"lineno":51},"order":2,"mdaics":{"dist":"packages/backend/dist/resources/model/gltf.js:36","src":"packages/backend/src/resources/model/gltf.ts:62"},"level":0},{"id":"writeGltfJson","longname":"writeGltfJson","name":"writeGltfJson","kind":"constant","scope":"global","description":"Converts a document to the glTF JSON document plus its resources.","params":[{"description":"The document to convert.","name":"document","type":{"names":["Document"]}}],"returns":[{"description":"The JSON document and the resource map.","type":{"names":["Promise<GltfJsonOutput>"]}}],"meta":{"lineno":60},"order":3,"mdaics":{"dist":"packages/backend/dist/resources/model/gltf.js:40","src":"packages/backend/src/resources/model/gltf.ts:72"},"level":0},{"id":"optimizeDocument","longname":"optimizeDocument","name":"optimizeDocument","kind":"constant","scope":"global","description":"Runs the optimize pipeline in the caller (used by the worker, where transforms are safe).","params":[{"description":"The document to optimize (already opened via {@link readModel}).","name":"document","type":{"names":["Document"]}},{"description":"Compression codec, simplification ratio and weld.","name":"options","type":{"names":["{ compress: \"draco\" | \"meshopt\" | \"none\"; simplify: number; weld: boolean; }"]}},{"description":"The compression codec ('meshopt', 'draco' or 'none').","name":"options.compress"},{"description":"The simplification ratio in [0, 1]; 1 disables it.","name":"options.simplify"},{"description":"Whether to weld bitwise-identical vertices.","name":"options.weld"}],"meta":{"lineno":73},"order":4,"mdaics":{"dist":"packages/backend/dist/resources/model/gltf.js:45","src":"packages/backend/src/resources/model/gltf.ts:86"},"returns":[{"type":{"names":["Promise<void>"]}}],"level":0}],"fp":"cc482a2cfe73015438e48136a55e7dd0b16d9ab7a704ecc66bc789a74c9abfe4","issues":[],"kind":"tdata","lastUsed":1795079891198,"symbols":0},"md:packages/backend/src/resources/model/gltf.ts":{"fp":"32652fcf192a7d1b7031e5145f7ffa8b6847995e14476f502f419d9022d1c273","issues":[],"kind":"md","markdown":"## Members\n\n<dl>\n<dt><a href=\"#ioPromise\">ioPromise</a></dt>\n<dd><p>Lazily-built NodeIO with meshopt and draco registered; wasm modules are created once per process.</p>\n</dd>\n</dl>\n\n## Constants\n\n<dl>\n<dt><a href=\"#readModel\">readModel</a> ⇒ <code>Promise&lt;Document&gt;</code></dt>\n<dd><p>Opens a GLB work package; a single corrupt byte answers 400.</p>\n</dd>\n<dt><a href=\"#writeGlb\">writeGlb</a> ⇒ <code>Promise&lt;Uint8Array&lt;ArrayBufferLike&gt;&gt;</code></dt>\n<dd><p>Serializes a document to GLB bytes.</p>\n</dd>\n<dt><a href=\"#writeGltfJson\">writeGltfJson</a> ⇒ <code>Promise&lt;GltfJsonOutput&gt;</code></dt>\n<dd><p>Converts a document to the glTF JSON document plus its resources.</p>\n</dd>\n<dt><a href=\"#optimizeDocument\">optimizeDocument</a> ⇒ <code>Promise&lt;void&gt;</code></dt>\n<dd><p>Runs the optimize pipeline in the caller (used by the worker, where transforms are safe).</p>\n</dd>\n</dl>\n\n<a name=\"ioPromise\"></a>\n\n## ioPromise\nLazily-built NodeIO with meshopt and draco registered; wasm modules are created once per process.\n\n**Kind**: global variable  \nsrc: packages/backend/src/resources/model/gltf.ts:18  \ndist: packages/backend/dist/resources/model/gltf.js:7\n<a name=\"readModel\"></a>\n\n## readModel ⇒ <code>Promise&lt;Document&gt;</code>\nOpens a GLB work package; a single corrupt byte answers 400.\n\n**Kind**: global constant  \n**Returns**: <code>Promise&lt;Document&gt;</code> - The parsed gltf-transform document.  \n\n| Param | Type | Description |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| buffer | <code>Buffer&lt;ArrayBufferLike&gt;</code> | The uploaded GLB bytes. |\n\nsrc: packages/backend/src/resources/model/gltf.ts:47  \ndist: packages/backend/dist/resources/model/gltf.js:27\n<a name=\"writeGlb\"></a>\n\n## writeGlb ⇒ <code>Promise&lt;Uint8Array&lt;ArrayBufferLike&gt;&gt;</code>\nSerializes a document to GLB bytes.\n\n**Kind**: global constant  \n**Returns**: <code>Promise&lt;Uint8Array&lt;ArrayBufferLike&gt;&gt;</code> - The GLB bytes.  \n\n| Param | Type | Description |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| document | <code>Document</code> | The document to serialize. |\n\nsrc: packages/backend/src/resources/model/gltf.ts:62  \ndist: packages/backend/dist/resources/model/gltf.js:36\n<a name=\"writeGltfJson\"></a>\n\n## writeGltfJson ⇒ <code>Promise&lt;GltfJsonOutput&gt;</code>\nConverts a document to the glTF JSON document plus its resources.\n\n**Kind**: global constant  \n**Returns**: <code>Promise&lt;GltfJsonOutput&gt;</code> - The JSON document and the resource map.  \n\n| Param | Type | Description |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| document | <code>Document</code> | The document to convert. |\n\nsrc: packages/backend/src/resources/model/gltf.ts:72  \ndist: packages/backend/dist/resources/model/gltf.js:40\n<a name=\"optimizeDocument\"></a>\n\n## optimizeDocument ⇒ <code>Promise&lt;void&gt;</code>\nRuns the optimize pipeline in the caller (used by the worker, where transforms are safe).\n\n**Kind**: global constant  \n\n| Param | Type | Description |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| document | <code>Document</code> | The document to optimize (already opened via [readModel](#readModel)). |\n| options | <code>{ compress: &quot;draco&quot; \\| &quot;meshopt&quot; \\| &quot;none&quot;; simplify: number; weld: boolean; }</code> | Compression codec, simplification ratio and weld. |\n| options.compress |  | The compression codec ('meshopt', 'draco' or 'none'). |\n| options.simplify |  | The simplification ratio in [0, 1]; 1 disables it. |\n| options.weld |  | Whether to weld bitwise-identical vertices. |\n\nsrc: packages/backend/src/resources/model/gltf.ts:86  \ndist: package