description":"The HTTP status that led here (401 or 503).","name":"props.reason"},{"description":"Called with the entered token; the parent stores it and refetches.","name":"props.onSubmit"}],"returns":[{"description":"The gate element.","type":{"names":["import(\"react\").JSX.Element"]}}],"meta":{"lineno":19},"order":0,"mdaics":{"src":"packages/dashboard/src/components/TokenGate.tsx:28"},"level":0}],"fp":"8be5d81d0f6cf0922c1345283e0192358d573ac0177a0d3b8b17b2637044a072","issues":[],"kind":"tdata","lastUsed":1795079894835,"symbols":0},"md:packages/dashboard/src/components/TokenGate.tsx":{"fp":"f9e8f6c6b11a3b3a05ab77634cc6aaabee1e1f76234123c06bef6ccb49cb7ee7","issues":["dist file not found — dist: line omitted (build first)"],"kind":"md","markdown":"<a name=\"TokenGate\"></a>\n\n## TokenGate(props) ⇒ <code>import(&quot;react&quot;).JSX.Element</code>\nShown when the backend refuses `/metrics`.\n\nTwo cases: 401 (the operator configured `METRICS_TOKEN`), where the user\nenters that token once per tab; and 503 (production without `METRICS_TOKEN`),\nwhich is a server misconfiguration the visitor cannot fix.\n\n**Kind**: global function  \n**Returns**: <code>import(&quot;react&quot;).JSX.Element</code> - The gate element.  \n\n| Param | Type | Description |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| props | <code>TokenGateProps</code> | Gate props. |\n| props.reason |  | The HTTP status that led here (401 or 503). |\n| props.onSubmit |  | Called with the entered token; the parent stores it and refetches. |\n\nsrc: packages/dashboard/src/components/TokenGate.tsx:28  \n","symbols":1,"lastUsed":1795079894867},"tdata:packages/dashboard/src/lib/api.spec.ts":{"doclets":[],"fp":"b3fd73e12cfacd6a9250ca98ccaa4bbc4eeef215a0dff8832552c80dde3bd1fb","issues":[],"kind":"tdata","lastUsed":1795079894846,"symbols":0},"md:packages/dashboard/src/lib/api.spec.ts":{"fp":"6580a875824913ab741c009f72c1ad400599fe0b0ed8a72245f67afc546b4b40","issues":["dist file not found — dist: line omitted (build first)"],"kind":