{"description":"The aggregated metrics snapshot.","type":{"names":["Promise<MetricsSnapshot>"]}}],"exceptions":[{"description":"ApiError When the backend answers with a non-2xx status."}],"meta":{"lineno":55},"order":5,"mdaics":{"src":"packages/dashboard/src/lib/api.ts:128"},"level":0},{"id":"ApiError#status","longname":"ApiError#status","name":"status","kind":"member","scope":"instance","description":"HTTP status code returned by the server.","memberof":"ApiError","meta":{"lineno":5},"order":0,"mdaics":{"src":"packages/dashboard/src/lib/api.ts:72"},"level":0}],"fp":"9e45561864204622a4403148bda1471a013bdfb7ac19decd6f8a969b2e84931e","issues":[],"kind":"tdata","lastUsed":1795079894867,"symbols":0},"md:packages/dashboard/src/lib/format.spec.ts":{"fp":"481c774f1860a16810b5ec40c75a90aa9901319fbf64f1827c662c1b283aea4d","issues":["dist file not found — dist: line omitted (build first)"],"kind":"md","skipped":"no-jsdoc","symbols":0,"lastUsed":1795079894913},"md:packages/dashboard/src/lib/api.ts":{"fp":"856822e0e89bb2189e470f8afe5918bffce7f27fc9d4717df9070428b00c85c3","issues":["dist file not found — dist: line omitted (build first)"],"kind":"md","markdown":"## Classes\n\n<dl>\n<dt><a href=\"#ApiError\">ApiError</a></dt>\n<dd><p>Error carrying the HTTP status returned by the backend.</p>\n</dd>\n</dl>\n\n## Functions\n\n<dl>\n<dt><a href=\"#metricsToken\">metricsToken()</a> ⇒ <code>string</code></dt>\n<dd><p>Reads the session token, when one was stored for this tab.</p>\n</dd>\n<dt><a href=\"#setMetricsToken\">setMetricsToken(token)</a></dt>\n<dd><p>Stores or clears the session token.</p>\n</dd>\n<dt><a href=\"#fetchMetrics\">fetchMetrics()</a> ⇒ <code>Promise&lt;MetricsSnapshot&gt;</code></dt>\n<dd><p>Fetches the current metrics snapshot.</p>\n<p>The dashboard polls, so there is deliberately no retry wrapper: the next\npoll is the retry. Failures surface as <code>ApiError</code> for 401/503 and render\nthe token gate / disabled banner.</p>\n</dd>\n</dl>\n\n<a name=\"ApiError\"></a>\n\n## ApiError\nError carrying the HTTP status returned by the backend.\n\n**Kind**: global class  \nsrc: packages/dashboard/src/lib/api.ts:70  \n\n* [ApiError](#ApiError)\n    * [new ApiError(status)](#new_ApiError_new)\n    * [.status](#ApiError+status)\n\n<a name=\"new_ApiError_new\"></a>\n\n### new ApiError(status)\nCreates an ApiError.\n\n\n| Param | Type | Description |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| status | <code>number</code> | HTTP status code returned by the server. |\n\n<a name=\"ApiError+status\"></a>\n\n### apiError.status\nHTTP status code returned by the server.\n\n**Kind**: instance property of [<code>ApiError</code>](#ApiError)  \nsrc: packages/dashboard/src/lib/api.ts:72  \n<a name=\"metricsToken\"></a>\n\n## metricsToken() ⇒ <code>string</code>\nReads the session token, when one was stored for this tab.\n\n**Kind**: global function  \n**Returns**: <code>string</code> - The stored token, or undefined.  \nsrc: packages/dashboard/src/lib/api.ts:92  \n<a name=\"setMetricsToken\"></a>\n\n## setMetricsToken(token)\nStores or clears the session token.\n\n**Kind**: global function  \n\n| Param | Type | Description |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| token | <code>string</code> | Token to store, or undefined/empty to clear it. |\n\nsrc: packages/dashboard/src/lib/api.ts:100  \n<a name=\"fetchMetrics\"></a>\n\n## fetchMetrics() ⇒ <code>Promise&lt;MetricsSnapshot&gt;</code>\nFetches the current metrics snapshot.\n\nThe dashboard polls, so there is deliberately no retry wrapper: the next\npoll is the retry. Failures surface as `ApiError` for 401/503 and render\nthe token gate / disabled banner.\n\n**Kind**: global function  \n**Returns**: <code>Promise&lt;MetricsSnapshot&gt;</code> - The aggregated metrics snapshot.  \n**Throws**:\n\n- ApiError When the backend answers with a non-2xx status.\n\nsrc: packages/dashboard/src/lib/api.ts:128  \n","symbols":6,"lastUsed":1795079894909},"tdata:packages/dashboard/src/lib/format.ts":{"doclets":[{"id":"formatBytes","longname":"formatBytes","name":"formatBytes","kind":"function","scope":"global","description":"Formats a byte count with binary (1024) units.","params":[{"description":"Size in bytes; non-finite or negative values format as `0 B`.","name":"bytes","type":{"names":["number"]}}],"returns":[{"description":"Human-readable string such as `1.5 GB`.","type":{"names":["string"]}}],"meta":{"lineno":6},"order":0,"mdaics":{"src":"packages/dashboard/src/lib/format.ts:6"},"level":0},{"id":"formatCount","longname":"formatCount","name":"formatCount","kind":"function","scope":"global","description":"Formats a count with thousands separators.","params":[{"description":"The count to format.","name":"value","type":{"names":["number"]}}],"returns":[{"description":"Locale-formatted string such as `1,234,567`.","type":{"names":["string"]}}],"meta":{"lineno":25},"order":1,"mdaics":{"src":"packages/dashboard/src/lib/format.ts:21"},"level":0},{"id":"formatHourBucket","longname":"formatHourBucket","name":"formatHourBucket","kind":"function","scope":"global","description":"Turns an ISO hour bucket into an axis label like `11-17 14:00`.","params":[{"description":"ISO hour bucket, e.g. `2026-11-17T14`.","name":"bucket","type":{"names":["string"]}}],"returns":[{"description":"Day and hour, e.g. `11-17 14:00`; `00:00` for malformed input.","type":{"names":["string"]}}],"meta":{"lineno":33},"order":2,"mdaics":{"src":"packages/dashboard/src/lib/format.ts:30"},"level":0},{"id":"formatMs","longname":"formatMs","name":"formatMs","kind":"function","scope":"global","description":"Formats a duration given in milliseconds.","params":[{"description":"Duration in milliseconds; non-finite or negative values format as `0 ms`.","name":"ms","type":{"names":["number"]}}],"returns":[{"description":"String such as `12.3 ms`.","type":{"names":["string"]}}],"meta":{"lineno":44},"order":3,"mdaics":{"src":"packages/dashboard/src/lib/format.ts:41"},"level":0},{"id":"formatPercent","longname":"formatPercent","name":"formatPercent","kind":"function","scope":"global","description":"Formats a ratio as a percentage.","params":[{"description":"Value in the range [0, 1].","name":"ratio","type":{"names":["number"]}},{"description":"Number of decimals to show.","name":"digits","type":{"names":["number"]}}],"returns":[{"description":"Percent string such as `87.5%`, or `0%` for non-finite input.","type":{"names":["string"]}}],"meta":{"lineno":57},"order":4,"mdaics":{"src":"packages/dashboard/src/lib/format.ts:53"},"level":0}],"fp":"8e580690bead26d2e9edfadefa722a72a5e2f43e0f850ebf3d4f84d4709c6d22","issues":[],"kind":"tdata","lastUsed":1795079894913,"symbols":0},"md:packages/dashboard/src/lib/format.ts":{"fp":"214b73093a6c58fd99f670a8d24c4fc744004a8e598469a645791a1ba30a6e9f","issues":["dist file not found — dist: line omitted (build first)"],"kind":"md","markdown":"## Functions\n\n<dl>\n<dt><a href=\"#formatBytes\">formatBytes(bytes)</a> ⇒ <code>string</code></dt>\n<dd><p>Formats a byte count with binary (1024) units.</p>\n</dd>\n<dt><a href=\"#formatCount\">formatCount(value)</a> ⇒ <code>string</code></dt>\n<dd><p>Formats a count with thousands separators.</p>\n</dd>\n<dt><a href=\"#formatHourBucket\">formatHourBucket(bucket)</a> ⇒ <code>string</code></dt>\n<dd><p>Turns an ISO hour bucket into an axis label like <code>11-17 14:00</code>.</p>\n</dd>\n<dt><a href=\"#formatMs\">formatMs(ms)</a> ⇒ <code>string</code></dt>\n<dd><p>Formats a duration given in milliseconds.</p>\n</dd>\n<dt><a href=\"#formatPercent\">formatPercent(ratio, digits)</a> ⇒ <code>string</code></dt>\n<dd><p>Formats a ratio as a percentage.</p>\n</dd>\n</dl>\n\n<a name=\"formatBytes\"></a>\n\n## formatBytes(bytes) ⇒ <code>string</code>\nFormats a byte count with binary (1024) units.\n\n**Kind**: global function  \n**Returns**: <code>string</code> - Human-readable string such as `1.5 GB`.  \n\n| Param | Type | Description |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| bytes | <code>number</code> | Size in bytes; non-finite or negative values format as `0 B`. |\n\nsrc: packages/dashboard/src/lib/format.ts:6  \n<a name=\"formatCount\"></a>\n\n## formatCount(value) ⇒ <code>string</code>\nFormats a count with thousands separators.\n\n**Kind**: global function  \n**Returns**: <code>string</code> - Locale-formatted string such as `1,234,567`.  \n\n| Param | Type | Description |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| value | <code>number</code> | The count to format. |\n\nsrc: packages/dashboard/src/lib/format.ts:21  \n<a name=\"formatHourBucket\"></a>\n\n## formatHourBucket(bucket) ⇒ <code>string</code>\nTurns an ISO hour bucket into an axis label like `11-17 14:00`.\n\n**Kind**: global function  \n**Returns**: <code>string</code> - Day and hour, e.g. `11-17 14:00`; `00:00` for malformed input.  \n\n| Param | Type | Description |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| bucket | <code>string</code> | ISO hour bucket, e.g. `2026-11-17T14`. |\n\nsrc: packages/dashboard/src/lib/format.ts:30  \n<a name=\"formatMs\"></a>\n\n## formatMs(ms) ⇒ <code>string</code>\nFormats a duration given in milliseconds.\n\n**Kind**: global function  \n**Returns**: <code>string</code> - String such as `12.3 ms`.  \n\n| Param | Type | Description |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| ms | <code>number</code> | Duration in milliseconds; non-finite or negative values format as `0 ms`. |\n\nsrc: packages/dashboard/src/lib/format.ts:41  \n<a name=\"formatPercent\"></a>\n\n## formatPercent(ratio, digits) ⇒ <code>string</code>\nFormats a ratio as a percentage.\n\n**Kind**: global function  \n**Returns**: <code>string</code> - Percent string such as `87.5%`, or `0%` for non-finite input.  \n\n| Param | Type | Description |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| ratio | <code>number</code> | Value in the range [0, 1]. |\n| digits | <code>number</code> | Number of decimals to show. |\n\nsrc: packages/dashboard/src/lib/format.ts:53  \n","symbols":5,"lastUsed":1795079894951},"tdata:packages/dashboard/src/main.tsx":{"doclets":[],"fp":"cc24e1e5b4edf2f917782da9a2d6005a898f1e8b542bc6f0ac55e51ecbb69ad6","issues":[],"kin